# Stage a before/after screen for the TRUE_SIGHT fix (bead inc-5bl3): True
# Seeing is supposed to let the caster see an invisible creature AND see
# through darkness, out to 12 squares (lib/wspells.irh:9160-9179). This is
# the gameplay observation the project's before/after rule asks for -- a
# rendered screen, not a probe.
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#   INCURSION_RUN_DIR=logs/runs/tsobs-<something-unique> \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/true-sight-observe.keys <seed>
#
# WHAT IT STAGES. A mage (chargen-mage.keys) learns True Seeing through
# wizard mode's "Learn Any Spell", then wizard mode summons a sprite
# adjacent to him. The sprite (lib/mon2.irh:3031) carries
# Stati[INVIS,INV_IMPROVED], so it is invisible with no extra step. The
# session dumps the screen once with the sprite present and True Seeing not
# yet cast, casts the spell on himself, and dumps again.
#
# WHY THE SCENE MOVES TO DEPTH 2 FIRST. The Entry Chamber the mage arrives in
# is a fixed, hand-authored room (lib/dungeon.irh:4098, RF_NOGEN) whose own
# text says the goblins' runes read "light" and "surface" -- it is lit by
# design, and Creature::DoTurn (src/Creature.cpp:1350-1359) confirms it:
# standing there fires the M_LIGHT_AVERSE "You squint and stagger in the
# bright light" message on the very first turn. Wizard mode's "Ascend /
# Descend Depth" (case 15, src/Debug.cpp) generates depth 2 on the spot and
# drops the character into it -- an ordinary procedurally-built level, with
# none of the Entry Chamber's scripted light. Measured on seed 1: only about
# six squares of corridor show on either side of the player before the cast.
#
# WHY INFINITE MANA. True Seeing is learned with SP_KNOWN|SP_PRIMAL|SP_INNATE
# (src/Debug.cpp:861, wizard case 17), and an innate cast dispatches through
# EV_INVOKE rather than EV_CAST (src/Player.cpp:828-830), but Infinite Mana is
# switched on anyway so the cast cannot fail for want of mana on a level-1
# mage holding a level-6 spell.
#
# WHY FREEZE MONSTERS, AND WHY NOT WIZARD SIGHT. Freeze Monsters (the 11th
# switch) holds the sprite still between the two dumps, so nothing about the
# scene changes except the cast. Wizard Sight (the 10th switch) is left OFF
# on purpose: it would light the whole screen for the player and erase the
# very darkness this script exists to show.
#
# WHY "Faerie" FINDS THE SPRITE WITH ONE ANSWER. The monster-summoning
# category menu only offers a group for a monster type inside
# 1..MA_LAST_REAL (src/Term.cpp:2885-2890, inc/Defines.h:1608). Of the
# sprite's three types -- MA_FAERIE (9), MA_SYLVAN (81), MA_COUTSIDER (118)
# -- only MA_FAERIE is in range, so "Faerie" is the one category the sprite
# can appear under. Inside it, @choose "sprite" cannot land on "rainbow
# sprite" instead: FindMenuEntry only accepts a PREFIX match
# (src/Wposix.cpp:901-913), and "sprite" is not a prefix of "rainbow
# sprite".
#
# WHY NO TARGET PROMPT ON THE CAST. True Seeing's clause carries no qval
# (lib/wspells.irh:9160-9179), and Magic.cpp treats an untargeted cast with
# qval == 0 as self-targeted (src/Magic.cpp:2852-2856), so 'm' -> @choose
# "True Seeing" fires with no further keystroke.

@include chargen-mage.keys

# chargen-mage.keys usually ends with the arrival room description still on
# screen (its own last comment: "the next keystroke dismisses" it), but not
# on every seed -- on seed 4242 the three starting-spell picks ('a a a')
# already used up that dismissal, because that character was offered fewer
# than three. A bare ESC then hits ordinary play and opens the System Menu
# instead (ESC's other job -- see tools/keys/explore-mage.keys), which is
# exactly the failure this line exists to avoid. "mass grave" is a phrase
# from the Entry Chamber's own description (lib/dungeon.irh:4101-4102) that
# appears nowhere else on screen, so @while presses ESC only while the box
# showing it is actually still up.
@while "mass grave" ESC

# Wizard switches: Infinite Mana is the 8th, Freeze Monsters the 11th.
w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*7
SPACE
DOWN*3
SPACE
ESC

# Off the lit Entry Chamber and onto an ordinary depth-2 level; see header.
w
@choose "Ascend / Descend Depth"
"2"
ENTER

# Landing inside a NAMED special room (Move.cpp:1626-1642) pops up that
# room's own description box before the "Done." message that always follows
# a successful jump; landing in a plain corridor skips the box entirely. The
# box swallows any non-arrow key, so @until presses one only if "Done." is
# not already on screen -- zero presses when there was no box, one when
# there was.
@until "Done." w

# Learn True Seeing (wizard case 17, a free-text "Enter Spell Name:" prompt).
w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"True Seeing"
ENTER

# Summon an invisible sprite one square east of the player.
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Faerie"
@choose "sprite"
RIGHT
ENTER

@dump:before-trueseeing

# Cast True Seeing on the player -- no target prompt; see header.
m
@choose "True Seeing"
@while "more --" SPACE

@dump:after-trueseeing

@quit
